                'The Quran intercedes in two ways. First, by testifying to the good it produced in you. Reading the Quran changes the heart. It makes one softer, more honest, more generous, more patient. The Quran will point to these changes and say, "This is the fruit of my presence in their life." Second, by directly requesting Allah\'s mercy, which Allah grants because He loves His own words and He loves those who love His words.',
