                'To install on Android: open baca-al-qur-an.vercel.app in Chrome (or any modern browser). You will see an "Install App" banner in the footer, or you can open the browser menu (three dots in the top right) and select "Install app" or "Add to Home Screen." Confirm, and Baca will appear in your app drawer with its own icon. It will open in its own window, without the browser chrome, and will work offline.',
                'To install on iPhone (iOS): open the site in Safari. Tap the Share button (the square with the up arrow at the bottom). Scroll down and tap "Add to Home Screen." Tap Add. Baca will appear on your home screen with its own icon. When you tap it, it will open in standalone mode, without the Safari browser chrome, and will work offline for content you have previously loaded.',
                'To install on desktop (Windows, Mac, Linux): open the site in Chrome or Edge. You should see an "Install" icon in the address bar (a small monitor with a plus). Click it and confirm. Baca will be installed as a desktop app, accessible from your start menu / applications folder, and will run in its own window. This is useful for keeping your Quran reading separate from your browser tabs.',
                'Once installed, Baca behaves like a real app. It has its own icon, opens in its own window, and most importantly, the audio recitations you have played will be cached. So if you listen to Surah Al-Mulk every night before sleeping, the audio will be available even if your internet goes down. The Quran text itself is small and cached on first load, so the entire text is always available offline.',
                'There is one important difference between the web version and the installed app version. In the installed app (standalone mode), some sections are hidden because they are accessible via the mobile More sheet: topics, journeys, bookmarks, featured reciters, daily reflection, reading progress, daily challenge, and achievements. These are still available via the bottom tab bar and the More sheet. The web version shows everything at once; the installed app is more focused and minimal, designed for daily use on a phone.',
                'If you have been using Baca in your browser, consider installing it. The difference is small but meaningful. An installed app is one tap away. A browser tab is buried among dozens of other tabs. An installed app feels like yours. A browser bookmark feels like a reference. The Quran deserves a place on your home screen, not just in your bookmarks. Try it, and see if it changes your daily reading habit.'
